WEBVTT

00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:10.880
The history of gaming extends 5,000 
years into the past to ancient Egypt.

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:15.250
Ancient games foretold the 
futures of men and kings.

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:18.950
They were magic ceremonies that 
determined a person's fate.

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:22.930
These ceremonies were known 
as the "Shadow Games."

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:26.630
In the present, a young boy 
solves the Millennium Puzzle.

00:00:27.010 --> 00:00:29.960
He becomes the heir to the Shadow Games.

00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:38.050
This boy possesses two hearts - 
one of light and one of darkness.

00:00:38.570 --> 00:00:41.960
He is known as "Yu-Gi-Oh."

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:50.310
I can't finish reading the magazine pages

00:00:52.230 --> 00:00:57.220
I get the feeling that I must read it

00:00:59.110 --> 00:01:03.970
Game cartridges are stacked 
in the corner of the room

00:01:05.930 --> 00:01:10.670
Is there no meaning if I don't play them?

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:15.770
You're on the other side of the table

00:01:16.220 --> 00:01:19.140
I'm talking to you, but...

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:26.070
You don't change your 
facial expression at all

00:01:27.010 --> 00:01:32.320
Even though I'm this close to you

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:39.590
These feelings don't reach 
you, don't reach you

00:01:40.010 --> 00:01:46.330
What is truly precious?

00:01:50.050 --> 00:01:55.500
Exodia Lost

00:02:02.620 --> 00:02:07.340
Pegasus has the power to see 
into another person's soul.

00:02:07.340 --> 00:02:12.120
How can I win when he knows 
my hand and strategies?

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:13.810
But I have to try.

00:02:13.810 --> 00:02:15.950
It's my fault that he took Grandpa.

00:02:16.540 --> 00:02:18.520
I won't run away.

00:02:18.520 --> 00:02:22.540
I'm going to the Kingdom to 
get my dear Grandpa back.

00:02:22.540 --> 00:02:24.320
Just wait, Pegasus!

00:02:31.220 --> 00:02:35.130
Big brother, it's been awhile.  How are you?

00:02:35.130 --> 00:02:36.550
Shizuka.

00:02:36.860 --> 00:02:42.750
I sent you this video so that you 
wouldn't forget what I looked like.

00:02:43.060 --> 00:02:45.350
Jonouchi!

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:48.430
Shizuka!

00:02:50.590 --> 00:02:55.450
It's unfortunate for me that I can't see you.

00:02:56.230 --> 00:03:01.330
Instead of a video, I want 
to see you in person.

00:03:01.330 --> 00:03:04.980
I wanted to see your face one last time.

00:03:04.980 --> 00:03:06.670
One last time?

00:03:06.940 --> 00:03:08.470
Shizuka...

00:03:08.930 --> 00:03:11.950
Bye bye, Jonouchi.

00:03:15.330 --> 00:03:16.950
Damn!

00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:23.720
Huh?  What's this?

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:28.750
This is...

00:03:32.260 --> 00:03:34.490
It's an invitation to the Kingdom.

00:03:36.060 --> 00:03:37.500
You're going by boat?

00:03:37.660 --> 00:03:40.910
That means the event will 
take place on an island.

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:46.790
It says I'm leaving in a week 
from Domino Pier at 9:30 pm.

00:03:46.790 --> 00:03:49.480
It's an invitation to the Kingdom.

00:03:49.480 --> 00:03:52.210
Is your grandpa there?

00:03:52.210 --> 00:03:56.020
I don't know, but I have 
to go to this island.

00:03:56.020 --> 00:04:02.260
I can't believe he kidnapped your 
grandpa without us noticing.

00:04:02.260 --> 00:04:05.260
Pegasus is no ordinary person.

00:04:05.500 --> 00:04:09.580
Damn.  We can't get on the 
boat without an invitation.

00:04:09.580 --> 00:04:11.860
We can't do anything at all!

00:04:11.860 --> 00:04:13.350
Yeah.

00:04:14.160 --> 00:04:16.350
I wish we could go with you.

00:04:16.890 --> 00:04:18.620
Hey Yugi.

00:04:18.620 --> 00:04:21.590
This Glory of the King's Hand card says...

00:04:22.410 --> 00:04:25.240
...huge prize money.

00:04:25.240 --> 00:04:26.680
Prize money?

00:04:26.680 --> 00:04:30.530
The winner will get a large amount of money.

00:04:30.530 --> 00:04:32.710
Let me see!

00:04:33.260 --> 00:04:34.740
You're right.

00:04:34.740 --> 00:04:36.600
Jonouchi?

00:04:36.600 --> 00:04:39.230
Huge prize money.

00:04:45.540 --> 00:04:47.110
Jonouchi.

00:04:47.940 --> 00:04:49.420
What's wrong?

00:04:49.420 --> 00:04:53.750
Look.  The sunset is really red.

00:04:53.750 --> 00:04:58.010
Yugi, your grandpa taught 
me the heart of dueling.

00:04:58.260 --> 00:05:00.640
I'm grateful for that.

00:05:00.640 --> 00:05:02.480
Jonouchi.

00:05:02.480 --> 00:05:06.150
Don't lose!  You have to 
get your grandpa back!

00:05:07.660 --> 00:05:11.820
I'm really happy that I met you, Jonouchi.

00:05:11.820 --> 00:05:13.750
What's gotten into you?

00:05:14.090 --> 00:05:18.550
Remember when I was assembling this 
Millennium Puzzle that Grandpa gave me?

00:05:19.960 --> 00:05:21.830
This is my treasure.

00:05:21.830 --> 00:05:25.650
They found this Puzzle 
in some Egyptian ruins.

00:05:25.650 --> 00:05:29.500
I don't know what it'll look like 
because I haven't put it together yet.

00:05:29.500 --> 00:05:33.240
So it's something I can 
see but remains unseen.

00:05:33.240 --> 00:05:38.700
I wished upon the Puzzle 
that I wanted a best friend.

00:05:38.700 --> 00:05:42.260
I felt the Millennium Puzzle 
would make my wish come true.

00:05:42.260 --> 00:05:45.870
That's when I met you and Honda.

00:05:47.380 --> 00:05:50.830
I made a horrible first impression.

00:05:51.260 --> 00:05:56.750
When I saw how timid you were, it annoyed me.

00:06:00.770 --> 00:06:02.670
Your treasure?

00:06:06.380 --> 00:06:10.460
Since I was being bullied, 
Ushio pretended to protect me.

00:06:10.460 --> 00:06:13.870
However, he was trying to extort money.

00:06:15.140 --> 00:06:16.220
Damn...

00:06:16.220 --> 00:06:20.500
Yugi, you need to pay up.

00:06:20.500 --> 00:06:23.130
Your bodyguard fee is 200,000 yen.

00:06:23.290 --> 00:06:25.160
What?

00:06:25.160 --> 00:06:30.180
This is your chance for payback.  Punch them!

00:06:30.180 --> 00:06:34.070
Stop it!  I won't hit my friends!

00:06:35.340 --> 00:06:37.070
You're so naïve.

00:06:37.070 --> 00:06:39.070
I'll hit you too!

00:06:43.220 --> 00:06:50.790
That's when I wanted - not just 
wished - for a best friend.

00:06:51.380 --> 00:06:57.270
You searched for the Puzzle 
piece that you threw away.

00:07:05.380 --> 00:07:09.020
Following your example, I decided 
to have my own treasure.

00:07:09.020 --> 00:07:11.270
Really?  Let me see.

00:07:12.390 --> 00:07:14.460
I can't show it to you because my treasure

00:07:14.460 --> 00:07:17.680
is also something that can be seen but remains unseen.

00:07:18.680 --> 00:07:25.430
It's friendship.  We can see each 
other, but we can't see friendship.

00:07:26.940 --> 00:07:31.390
Did I really say something that corny?

00:07:31.900 --> 00:07:34.570
I wish everyone could come with me.

00:07:34.570 --> 00:07:37.000
Don't be discouraged.

00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:40.300
Our hearts are always with you.

00:07:40.300 --> 00:07:41.620
That's right.

00:07:41.620 --> 00:07:44.530
That's right.  Be strong and go.

00:07:44.530 --> 00:07:46.830
I'll do my best.

00:07:51.700 --> 00:07:58.320
Chosen duelists, welcome to the event 
sponsored by Industrial Illusions.

00:07:58.320 --> 00:08:05.940
We observed your past Duel Monsters 
battles, and we selected you as the elite.

00:08:05.940 --> 00:08:09.350
You each have an equal chance of winning.

00:08:09.840 --> 00:08:15.140
The star of glory shines above your heads.

00:08:15.140 --> 00:08:20.810
Duelists, we will cross the ocean 
towards the Kingdom for glory!

00:08:23.820 --> 00:08:27.120
Present your Star Chips 
as you board the vessel.

00:08:27.120 --> 00:08:29.120
Thank you.  Good.

00:08:29.120 --> 00:08:30.860
Where are your Star Chips?

00:08:30.860 --> 00:08:33.620
C'mon, let it slide and let me on board.

00:08:33.620 --> 00:08:36.660
No!  Throw him out!

00:08:36.660 --> 00:08:39.980
Let me on!  I'm a friend of Yugi 
Muto, the guy who defeated Kaiba!

00:08:39.980 --> 00:08:41.420
Jonouchi?

00:08:41.420 --> 00:08:44.640
Leave quietly or else!

00:08:44.640 --> 00:08:47.420
Fine!  If you want to 
fight, I'll take you on!

00:08:47.420 --> 00:08:48.640
Wait!

00:08:48.640 --> 00:08:50.140
Hey, Yugi.

00:08:50.140 --> 00:08:51.380
Who are you?

00:08:51.380 --> 00:08:53.630
What are you doing here, Jonouchi?

00:08:54.020 --> 00:08:56.670
I was worried about you going alone.

00:08:58.180 --> 00:09:00.790
All right.

00:09:01.080 --> 00:09:02.390
Let's go.

00:09:03.180 --> 00:09:05.420
Let my friend come on board.

00:09:05.420 --> 00:09:07.100
We don't make exceptions.

00:09:07.100 --> 00:09:10.300
Only people with Star Chips can get on board.

00:09:10.300 --> 00:09:13.300
Jonouchi has a Star Chip.

00:09:13.300 --> 00:09:14.300
What?

00:09:14.300 --> 00:09:15.550
Here.

00:09:18.330 --> 00:09:19.300
This is...

00:09:19.800 --> 00:09:23.700
According to this card, a Star 
Chip proves that he's a duelist.

00:09:23.700 --> 00:09:27.720
That's true, but all participants 
are given two Star Chips.

00:09:27.720 --> 00:09:29.310
You'll be at a disadvantage.

00:09:29.310 --> 00:09:30.610
It's fine.

00:09:30.610 --> 00:09:35.720
It's more important to 
have Jonouchi by my side.

00:09:36.170 --> 00:09:37.460
Yugi.

00:09:37.460 --> 00:09:38.830
What should we do?

00:09:40.090 --> 00:09:43.070
Hello, it's me.  We have a situation.

00:09:43.070 --> 00:09:45.510
Slow.

00:09:47.260 --> 00:09:49.460
Don't touch me!

00:09:49.460 --> 00:09:50.870
Say what?

00:09:56.560 --> 00:09:58.580
I'm glad they let you on board.

00:09:58.580 --> 00:10:02.030
I guess Pegasus isn't all bad.

00:10:04.950 --> 00:10:08.390
Yugi, I owe you for the rest of my life.

00:10:08.900 --> 00:10:10.990
Don't worry about it.

00:10:30.280 --> 00:10:33.070
This is exciting.

00:10:34.020 --> 00:10:36.270
I can't believe it.

00:10:37.660 --> 00:10:42.150
You're the Yugi that 
everyone's talking about?

00:10:42.150 --> 00:10:44.650
What a babe!

00:10:44.650 --> 00:10:49.100
I'm amazed that such a 
little boy defeated Kaiba.

00:10:49.100 --> 00:10:51.170
You're famous.

00:10:51.170 --> 00:10:52.160
Thank you.

00:10:52.340 --> 00:10:58.110
I'm Yugi's friend and also a 
master duelist!  My name is Jo-

00:10:58.900 --> 00:11:05.260
I show no mercy in a duel, even 
if my opponent is a little boy.

00:11:05.260 --> 00:11:06.790
I'll crush you.

00:11:07.140 --> 00:11:09.150
I want to duel her.

00:11:09.500 --> 00:11:11.480
My name is Mai Kujaku.

00:11:11.480 --> 00:11:13.190
See you later, kid.

00:11:13.190 --> 00:11:14.820
What's up with that?

00:11:14.820 --> 00:11:18.580
We're here because we were worried, 
but they were both flirting!

00:11:18.580 --> 00:11:20.290
You're too loud!

00:11:20.290 --> 00:11:22.570
This is why men suck.

00:11:22.570 --> 00:11:24.630
Is this a joke?

00:11:25.640 --> 00:11:29.820
This is a luxury ship, so why 
do we have to sleep out here?

00:11:29.820 --> 00:11:31.020
You again?

00:11:31.020 --> 00:11:32.100
I know you have nicer rooms!

00:11:32.100 --> 00:11:35.390
What's the ruckus?

00:11:36.060 --> 00:11:38.780
You're Yugi, right?

00:11:38.780 --> 00:11:40.060
You two are...

00:11:40.060 --> 00:11:42.610
Insector Haga and Dinosaur Ryuzaki.

00:11:42.610 --> 00:11:48.620
Only the top finishers of a tournament 
like us get private rooms.

00:11:48.870 --> 00:11:52.150
Haga, congratulations on 
winning the last tournament.

00:11:52.540 --> 00:11:53.700
It was nothing.

00:11:53.700 --> 00:11:56.860
I went easy on him.

00:11:57.230 --> 00:12:00.500
We're going to win this 
tournament.  Right, Yugi?

00:12:00.500 --> 00:12:05.860
To tell you the truth, winning the last 
tournament didn't feel like much of an achievement.

00:12:05.860 --> 00:12:10.880
I can't call myself a champion 
until I defeat you and Kaiba.

00:12:11.040 --> 00:12:15.380
I'm sure I'll end up battling 
you at the Kingdom, Yugi.

00:12:15.380 --> 00:12:17.420
I'm looking forward to it.

00:12:17.420 --> 00:12:18.880
Same here.

00:12:19.250 --> 00:12:22.180
What?  He's just a little kid.

00:12:22.180 --> 00:12:27.470
Did you know that there will be 
new dueling rules at the Kingdom?

00:12:27.780 --> 00:12:29.060
New rules?

00:12:29.060 --> 00:12:35.500
I don't know the details, but it seems 
we'll need even better strategies.

00:12:35.500 --> 00:12:39.440
I'm not worried about the rules.

00:12:39.440 --> 00:12:43.260
It's either crush or be crushed.

00:12:43.260 --> 00:12:44.500
That's right.

00:12:44.500 --> 00:12:47.180
You have guts.  I like that.

00:12:47.180 --> 00:12:52.060
Thanks.  I'm going back to 
my private room to relax.

00:12:52.060 --> 00:12:55.100
Actually, I don't like him.  He's annoying!

00:12:55.100 --> 00:12:57.620
This room isn't so bad.

00:12:57.620 --> 00:12:58.340
What?

00:12:58.340 --> 00:12:59.990
Look.

00:13:00.230 --> 00:13:03.700
They're already trading cards.

00:13:03.700 --> 00:13:09.020
If you're here, you can trade your 
cards to strengthen your decks.

00:13:09.020 --> 00:13:12.550
You can also find out your 
opponents' strategies.

00:13:12.550 --> 00:13:14.640
Insector Haga is impressive.

00:13:14.640 --> 00:13:16.380
He figured this out instantly.

00:13:16.380 --> 00:13:19.420
Hi, I'm Jonouchi.  Show me your cards!

00:13:19.420 --> 00:13:21.380
This looks powerful!

00:13:21.580 --> 00:13:23.100
Jonouchi...

00:13:23.100 --> 00:13:27.940
You're in trouble if you don't 
trust your cards by now.

00:13:27.940 --> 00:13:30.110
If you'll excuse me...

00:13:30.980 --> 00:13:33.900
You must be joking!

00:13:33.900 --> 00:13:37.400
You can't expect a lady to share a 
room!  It doesn't even have a shower!

00:13:37.400 --> 00:13:39.820
These are the rules.

00:13:39.820 --> 00:13:41.180
Call your boss!

00:13:41.180 --> 00:13:45.700
If you keep acting like a spoiled 
brat, they'll throw you off the boat.

00:13:45.700 --> 00:13:46.910
Who are you?

00:13:47.100 --> 00:13:49.680
Why don't you come to my private room?

00:13:49.680 --> 00:13:51.980
That makes me happy!  Seriously?

00:13:52.180 --> 00:13:53.670
Seriously!

00:13:57.480 --> 00:13:59.100
I'm at my breaking point.

00:13:59.100 --> 00:14:01.220
If we don't hide, we'll get in trouble!

00:14:01.220 --> 00:14:04.680
But I can't hold it.  Where's the bathroom?

00:14:04.680 --> 00:14:07.270
Relieve yourself over there.

00:14:07.690 --> 00:14:11.060
You fool!  I'm not a boy!

00:14:15.780 --> 00:14:17.300
Bakura?

00:14:18.140 --> 00:14:21.310
Is that Bakura?

00:14:21.310 --> 00:14:24.470
I'm not Ba-sure-a.

00:14:25.080 --> 00:14:26.810
What a lame joke.

00:14:27.060 --> 00:14:29.980
How do you like my private room?

00:14:29.980 --> 00:14:32.180
It's wonderful!

00:14:32.180 --> 00:14:35.030
Ryuzaki, you must be a strong duelist!

00:14:35.490 --> 00:14:36.710
Perhaps.

00:14:38.750 --> 00:14:43.270
I love strong men, especially 
ones that are stronger than me.

00:14:43.710 --> 00:14:45.500
Who do you think you're talking to?

00:14:45.500 --> 00:14:47.470
No one can beat me.

00:14:47.470 --> 00:14:49.700
Will you duel me?

00:14:49.700 --> 00:14:50.620
What?

00:14:50.620 --> 00:14:55.150
If you win, I'll do anything you say.

00:14:56.540 --> 00:14:58.780
I traded some cards.

00:14:58.780 --> 00:14:59.980
Show me.

00:14:59.980 --> 00:15:06.640
Salamandra, Kunai with Chain, 
Baby Dragon and Shield & Sword.

00:15:06.640 --> 00:15:10.860
With these spell cards, you'll 
have more strategies than before.

00:15:10.860 --> 00:15:11.620
I see.

00:15:11.620 --> 00:15:14.990
All right!  Now I'll win the tournament!

00:15:15.260 --> 00:15:18.500
I don't think it'll be that easy...  Oh yeah.

00:15:18.900 --> 00:15:20.640
Use this.

00:15:20.640 --> 00:15:23.140
It should help in an emergency.

00:15:24.340 --> 00:15:26.940
Okay.  Thanks!

00:15:26.940 --> 00:15:28.830
Hi Yugi.

00:15:29.260 --> 00:15:30.910
Haga?

00:15:31.780 --> 00:15:34.100
Shuffle the cards.

00:15:34.100 --> 00:15:36.450
Let's begin.

00:15:38.300 --> 00:15:40.990
Tonight is my lucky night!

00:15:43.340 --> 00:15:44.860
It's shuffled.

00:15:44.860 --> 00:15:48.730
I'll close my eyes and correctly guess 
all the cards, starting from the top.

00:15:48.980 --> 00:15:52.510
There's no way you can do that.

00:15:53.700 --> 00:15:56.590
The top card is Shadow of Eyes.

00:15:57.140 --> 00:15:58.460
What?

00:15:58.460 --> 00:15:59.740
That was luck.

00:15:59.980 --> 00:16:02.060
The second card is Harpie Lady.

00:16:02.060 --> 00:16:04.320
Then Elegant Egotist.

00:16:04.320 --> 00:16:06.750
Then Cyber Shield.

00:16:07.140 --> 00:16:09.350
Impossible...

00:16:10.700 --> 00:16:12.740
These are my card skills.

00:16:12.740 --> 00:16:16.900
I always know what cards I have 
and draw whichever one I want.

00:16:16.900 --> 00:16:18.790
Are you ready to duel?

00:16:18.790 --> 00:16:21.390
If you lose, leave this room.

00:16:21.980 --> 00:16:24.230
I'll take you on!

00:16:26.270 --> 00:16:29.180
The night breeze feels nice.

00:16:29.180 --> 00:16:31.740
Did you trade for any good cards?

00:16:31.740 --> 00:16:35.060
No.  I'll duel using the 
cards that I brought.

00:16:35.060 --> 00:16:36.670
I figured as much.

00:16:36.940 --> 00:16:42.620
Your deck contains the Exodia cards 
that you used to defeat Kaiba, right?

00:16:42.620 --> 00:16:43.780
You know about that.

00:16:43.780 --> 00:16:47.740
Can you let me see those legendary cards?

00:16:47.740 --> 00:16:50.340
If the secret is out, I 
don't need to hide them.

00:16:50.340 --> 00:16:53.310
I'm in trouble since you know my strategy.

00:16:54.130 --> 00:16:54.790
Here.

00:16:57.100 --> 00:17:00.380
So these are the Exodia cards.

00:17:00.380 --> 00:17:05.700
Yugi, I've been thinking of a strategy to 
defeat these cards for the longest time.

00:17:05.700 --> 00:17:08.310
But I couldn't come up with anything.

00:17:08.980 --> 00:17:11.110
Until now.

00:17:12.710 --> 00:17:14.700
This is how.

00:17:14.700 --> 00:17:16.030
What?

00:17:19.180 --> 00:17:21.830
Now no one can beat me!

00:17:22.270 --> 00:17:23.460
You punk!

00:17:23.460 --> 00:17:24.660
My cards!

00:17:24.820 --> 00:17:28.020
Grandpa gave me those precious cards!

00:17:28.020 --> 00:17:29.140
Damn it!

00:17:29.140 --> 00:17:30.670
Jonouchi!

00:17:32.140 --> 00:17:33.770
It's no use!

00:17:35.020 --> 00:17:37.400
Yugi, I promise to retrieve them.

00:17:37.620 --> 00:17:39.410
Come back to the ship!

00:17:39.640 --> 00:17:41.270
I promise to retrieve them.

00:17:41.670 --> 00:17:43.240
I found the first one!

00:17:43.240 --> 00:17:46.030
Your life is more valuable than those cards!

00:17:47.280 --> 00:17:51.430
There are things in this world that 
you have to risk your life to protect.

00:17:52.920 --> 00:17:55.940
Everyone has something that 
can never be replaced.

00:17:55.940 --> 00:17:59.750
Something valuable that you must never lose.

00:18:04.140 --> 00:18:05.800
Found it.  Just three more.

00:18:07.530 --> 00:18:09.170
Jonouchi!

00:18:12.460 --> 00:18:14.170
Jonouchi!

00:18:16.430 --> 00:18:18.540
Yugi, just three more.

00:18:18.540 --> 00:18:19.990
Jonouchi!

00:18:24.340 --> 00:18:26.420
I have to get the remaining cards...

00:18:26.420 --> 00:18:27.400
Yugi!

00:18:27.400 --> 00:18:28.830
Are you okay?

00:18:31.300 --> 00:18:32.580
Grab it!

00:18:32.580 --> 00:18:33.430
Hurry!

00:18:33.620 --> 00:18:35.930
Anzu!  Honda!

00:18:35.930 --> 00:18:37.860
Get out, loser!

00:18:37.860 --> 00:18:40.000
That was easy.

00:18:42.420 --> 00:18:43.840
You saved us.

00:18:43.840 --> 00:18:45.780
But why did you sneak on board?

00:18:45.780 --> 00:18:48.460
We were worried.

00:18:48.460 --> 00:18:50.040
Because you'd be alone.

00:18:50.040 --> 00:18:52.050
Thanks, everyone.

00:18:52.050 --> 00:18:54.010
I'm sorry, Yugi.

00:18:54.460 --> 00:18:57.460
I only found two of your cards.

00:18:57.460 --> 00:18:59.100
It's okay, Jonouchi.

00:18:59.100 --> 00:19:00.650
It's not okay.

00:19:00.650 --> 00:19:02.580
It's always the same for me.

00:19:02.580 --> 00:19:05.110
I never can help anyone.

00:19:05.410 --> 00:19:07.300
Not even my younger sister, Shizuka.

00:19:07.300 --> 00:19:08.540
Sister?

00:19:08.540 --> 00:19:11.090
Jonouchi, you have a sister?

00:19:11.090 --> 00:19:13.900
Our parents divorced when we were young.

00:19:13.900 --> 00:19:16.670
She lives far away with my mother.

00:19:17.040 --> 00:19:20.030
My sister was born with bad eyesight.

00:19:21.100 --> 00:19:22.940
She'll eventually become blind.

00:19:22.940 --> 00:19:24.540
Blind?

00:19:25.220 --> 00:19:28.190
She sent me a video a few days ago.

00:19:28.620 --> 00:19:32.750
I wanted to see your face one last time.

00:19:34.260 --> 00:19:37.230
The doctor probably told her that it's time.

00:19:37.500 --> 00:19:40.390
Her disease is even difficult 
to repair with surgery.

00:19:40.390 --> 00:19:45.770
There's a specialist in Germany with the 
latest equipment who can do the procedure.

00:19:45.770 --> 00:19:47.700
If he can perform her surgery...

00:19:47.700 --> 00:19:50.700
But I don't have the money 
to pay for the operation.

00:19:50.700 --> 00:19:52.640
That's why I have to win.

00:19:52.640 --> 00:19:58.810
The only way to help Shizuka is to win 
at the Kingdom and get the prize money.

00:20:05.020 --> 00:20:10.990
Jonouchi, let's do our best to 
save your sister and my grandpa.

00:20:11.780 --> 00:20:14.140
That's right.  Keep your spirits up.

00:20:14.140 --> 00:20:15.910
Look!  The island!

00:20:17.700 --> 00:20:20.950
That's Duelist Kingdom.

00:20:21.980 --> 00:20:27.710
Insector Haga, I'll defeat 
you first at the Kingdom!

00:20:31.510 --> 00:20:35.120
We finally arrive at 
Pegasus's Duelist Kingdom.

00:20:35.120 --> 00:20:40.440
After two days of dueling, only those who 
gather 10 Star Chips can enter the finals.

00:20:40.440 --> 00:20:45.320
Yugi, defeat that cheater 
Insector Haga first!

00:20:45.320 --> 00:20:49.230
We're led into the forest where 
a duel ring suddenly appears.

00:20:49.400 --> 00:20:52.080
Why is Haga laughing so confidently?

00:20:52.080 --> 00:20:54.870
He must be up to something again!

00:20:54.870 --> 00:20:57.320
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
Insector Combo

00:20:57.320 --> 00:20:59.370
Duel, standby!

00:21:01.360 --> 00:21:09.760
The flask glistens

00:21:10.800 --> 00:21:17.610
Wait for me in the science classroom

00:21:18.100 --> 00:21:26.590
If we put our cold hands together

00:21:27.280 --> 00:21:34.350
And rub them together, they become warm

00:21:36.060 --> 00:21:40.190
Shower of happiness

00:21:40.430 --> 00:21:44.300
I will shower you with it

00:21:44.530 --> 00:21:52.570
I will support you even when you feel lonely

00:21:52.780 --> 00:21:56.810
Shower of happiness

00:21:57.080 --> 00:22:00.940
You are not alone

00:22:01.320 --> 00:22:07.660
You're protected by a 
giant ring of friendship
